Set-Location -LiteralPath $PSScriptRoot
$msg = 'brand: the platform row is now the single source of brand presentation. Brand data lived in four unsynchronised places that never read the database - BRAND_IDENTITY in appointment_invites, _BRAND_MAP in branding_router, BRAND_CONFIG in frontend theme.js, and a pre-bundle IIFE in index.html - so adding a brand meant editing four files, and they had already drifted: EvoSys Pro accent was 087cff in two and 1d4ed8 in the third, BookaBoost was c9973d in the frontend and 2fb6ff in the branding API with no consumer to notice the difference. Adds fourteen nullable presentation columns to platforms plus app/services/brand_config.py as the one resolver: the database wins FIELD BY FIELD rather than row by row, so a half configured brand still renders, and a frozen copy of the old literals answers only for a deployment whose columns are not backfilled. auto_migrate backfills the exact values that were live, using COALESCE so it only ever fills a NULL and can never overwrite a colour someone chose in the product. branding_router loses its hostname table and answers from the resolver, appointment_invites resolves the brand from the row before the literal - BookaBoost invites previously signed AdvisorFlow because BRAND_IDENTITY only ever had an evosyspro entry - and public_identity level three now reads the database at all three call sites. The frontend hydrates from GET /branding and caches the answer, so every load after the first is database driven; the compiled in table survives only as a labelled first paint bootstrap because a fetch cannot beat the first frame and a flash of the wrong brand is worse than a literal. Deliberately NOT consolidated: the data-theme blocks in index.css, roughly forty custom properties and twenty eight component overrides per brand. That is a stylesheet, not configuration - the row says WHICH theme a brand uses, the stylesheet says what it looks like. Gate 25 proves both brands are byte for byte unchanged on both the frozen and database paths, and that a brand existing only as a row - no code entry anywhere - gets its name, mark, colours, tagline, favicon, title and domain from that row alone.'
& "$PSScriptRoot\deploy.ps1" -Message $msg
Write-Output ("DEPLOY_EXIT=" + $LASTEXITCODE)
